-- Seed the 10 finalized Insights blog posts from the client's master-page
-- handoff. Bodies are stored as HTML (the /insights/[slug] renderer uses
-- dangerouslySetInnerHTML). author_id / hero_image_id stay NULL, matching the
-- existing article seeds — real staff bylines + hero imagery are a follow-up
-- (README: confirm bylines with the client before publishing). Idempotent via
-- ON CONFLICT (slug). Dollar-quoted literals avoid apostrophe escaping.
insert into public.articles
  (id, slug, title, excerpt, category, status, body_html, read_minutes, published_at, created_at, updated_at)
values
(gen_random_uuid(), 'abu-dhabi-property-sales-h1-2026',
 $t$Abu Dhabi Property Sales Surge in H1 2026$t$,
 $e$Abu Dhabi property sales reached AED 84.49 billion in H1 2026, driven by strong off-plan demand and rising buyer confidence.$e$,
 'market_report', 'published',
 $html$<p>Abu Dhabi's property market continued its strong performance in the first half of 2026, recording AED 84.49 billion in apartment and villa sales across 16,585 residential transactions. The figures highlight a major rise in buyer activity and reinforce Abu Dhabi's position as one of the UAE's most resilient and attractive real estate markets.</p><p>A key driver of this growth has been off-plan demand. Off-plan sales accounted for 78% of transactions in H1 2026, showing that buyers and investors are continuing to respond to new launches, flexible payment plans, and long-term growth opportunities.</p><p>The market's momentum has also been supported by rising prices. Median apartment prices reached AED 1,927 per square foot, while villa prices climbed to AED 1,500 per square foot, reflecting stronger demand across both apartment and villa communities.</p><p>This growth is especially important for investors. High transaction volumes, strong off-plan activity, and continued development across major communities suggest that Abu Dhabi is attracting both end-users and long-term buyers. Communities such as Al Reem Island, Yas Island, Saadiyat Island, Hudayriyat Island, and Al Raha Beach remain central to this demand.</p><p>For buyers, the current market offers a wide range of options, from ready-to-move homes to new off-plan developments. For sellers, stronger transaction activity can support improved pricing, especially in high-demand communities. For investors, the market continues to offer opportunities linked to rental demand, capital appreciation, and future community growth.</p><p>As Abu Dhabi's property sector continues to expand, buyers should focus on location, developer reputation, payment structure, service charges, and long-term demand before making a decision. With the right guidance, the current market offers strong opportunities for both lifestyle buyers and investors.</p>$html$,
 6, '2026-07-06'::timestamptz, '2026-07-06'::timestamptz, '2026-07-06'::timestamptz),

(gen_random_uuid(), 'why-off-plan-properties-are-leading-abu-dhabi-market',
 $t$Why Off-Plan Properties Are Leading Abu Dhabi's Real Estate Market$t$,
 $e$Off-plan properties accounted for 78% of Abu Dhabi sales in H1 2026. Here's why buyers and investors are choosing new developments.$e$,
 'buyers_guide', 'published',
 $html$<p>Off-plan properties have become one of the strongest segments in Abu Dhabi's real estate market. In H1 2026, off-plan sales accounted for 78% of all residential transactions, showing clear demand for new projects and future-focused communities.</p><p>One of the main reasons buyers choose off-plan properties is flexibility. Many developers offer structured payment plans, allowing buyers to pay in stages rather than making a full payment upfront. This can make off-plan properties attractive to investors, first-time buyers, and end-users planning ahead.</p><p>Another major advantage is access to new communities. Abu Dhabi is seeing continued development across key locations, including Hudayriyat Island, Yas Island, Saadiyat Island, Al Reem Island, and Masdar City. These communities are attracting buyers looking for modern layouts, lifestyle amenities, waterfront access, green spaces, and long-term value.</p><p>Off-plan properties may also offer capital growth potential. Buyers who enter early in a project may benefit from price appreciation as construction progresses and the surrounding community develops. This is one reason off-plan investments remain popular among investors seeking medium- to long-term returns.</p><p>However, buyers should approach off-plan purchases carefully. It is important to check the developer's track record, project registration, escrow arrangements, payment plan, handover timeline, service charges, and resale conditions before committing. Abu Dhabi has strengthened its off-plan framework through regulated escrow accounts and digital processes designed to improve transparency and buyer protection.</p><p>For investors, off-plan properties can be a strong option when selected correctly. The best opportunities are usually found in locations with strong infrastructure, growing demand, reliable developers, and a clear future vision.</p>$html$,
 7, '2026-07-02'::timestamptz, '2026-07-02'::timestamptz, '2026-07-02'::timestamptz),

(gen_random_uuid(), 'abu-dhabi-top-performing-real-estate-areas-2026',
 $t$Abu Dhabi's Top Performing Real Estate Areas in 2026$t$,
 $e$Discover the top Abu Dhabi real estate areas in 2026, including Hudayriyat Island, Al Reem Island, Saadiyat Island, and Yas Island.$e$,
 'market_report', 'published',
 $html$<p>Abu Dhabi's real estate growth in 2026 has been driven by strong activity across several key communities. According to ADREC's Q1 2026 data, total real estate transactions reached AED 66 billion across 13,518 transactions, with Hudayriyat Island, Al Reem Island, and Saadiyat Island among the leading areas by transaction value.</p><p>Hudayriyat Island emerged as the top-performing area in Q1 2026, recording AED 11.97 billion in transactions. This reflects growing interest in large-scale master-planned communities, waterfront living, and luxury residential development.</p><p>Al Reem Island continued to perform strongly, recording AED 9.45 billion in transactions in Q1 2026. The island remains one of Abu Dhabi's most active residential destinations, especially for apartments, rental demand, and investor-focused purchases.</p><p>Saadiyat Island also remained a major market driver, recording AED 8.8 billion in Q1 2026 transactions. Known for luxury residences, cultural landmarks, beachfront communities, and premium developments, Saadiyat continues to attract high-end buyers and long-term investors.</p><p>Yas Island remains another key area, supported by its lifestyle attractions, family communities, entertainment destinations, and continuous residential development. Aldar's launch of Yas Park Place further highlights the ongoing demand for new homes in the heart of Yas Island.</p><p>For buyers, each area offers a different type of opportunity. Hudayriyat is emerging as a future-focused destination. Al Reem is strong for apartment living and rental demand. Saadiyat is ideal for luxury and beachfront buyers. Yas Island appeals to lifestyle-focused residents and investors.</p>$html$,
 8, '2026-06-28'::timestamptz, '2026-06-28'::timestamptz, '2026-06-28'::timestamptz),

(gen_random_uuid(), 'hudayriyat-island-real-estate-hotspot',
 $t$Hudayriyat Island Emerges as a Major Abu Dhabi Real Estate Hotspot$t$,
 $e$Hudayriyat Island is becoming one of Abu Dhabi's strongest real estate destinations, supported by major development and strong transaction value.$e$,
 'field_note', 'published',
 $html$<p>Hudayriyat Island has become one of the most talked-about real estate destinations in Abu Dhabi. In Q1 2026, the island recorded AED 11.97 billion in real estate transactions, making it the top-performing area in Abu Dhabi during that period.</p><p>This performance reflects the growing importance of Hudayriyat as a master-planned lifestyle destination. The island is being positioned as a major residential, leisure, sports, and waterfront community, offering a mix of villas, apartments, mansions, and lifestyle-led developments.</p><p>One of the reasons Hudayriyat is gaining attention is its long-term potential. Buyers are not only looking at the properties themselves, but also at the wider community vision. Large-scale infrastructure, waterfront planning, leisure facilities, and premium residential offerings all contribute to the island's growing appeal.</p><p>For investors, Hudayriyat offers exposure to one of Abu Dhabi's most ambitious future destinations. As more phases are launched and community infrastructure develops, the area may continue to attract strong demand from both local and international buyers.</p><p>For end-users, the appeal lies in lifestyle. Hudayriyat offers the potential for spacious homes, waterfront views, privacy, outdoor living, and access to future leisure and community facilities. This makes it especially attractive to families and luxury buyers looking for something different from established urban areas.</p><p>The strong transaction value recorded in Q1 2026 shows that Hudayriyat is no longer just an emerging area. It is becoming a central part of Abu Dhabi's next phase of real estate growth.</p>$html$,
 5, '2026-06-24'::timestamptz, '2026-06-24'::timestamptz, '2026-06-24'::timestamptz),

(gen_random_uuid(), 'tara-park-off-plan-al-reem-island',
 $t$Tara Park Brings New Off-Plan Opportunities to Al Reem Island$t$,
 $e$Tara Park by Modon adds 834 modern apartments to Al Reem Island, strengthening one of Abu Dhabi's most in-demand communities.$e$,
 'off_plan_watch', 'published',
 $html$<p>Al Reem Island continues to be one of Abu Dhabi's strongest residential markets, and Tara Park by Modon adds another important off-plan opportunity to the area. The project offers one, two, and three-bedroom apartments with a 40/60 payment plan and planned handover in Q2 2030.</p><p>Tara Park is positioned around modern city living, convenience, and access to key Abu Dhabi destinations. Al Reem Island is already known for its apartment communities, waterfront setting, retail access, schools, and proximity to major business districts.</p><p>For buyers, the project offers the advantage of entering a well-known and high-demand area through a new development. Al Reem Island has long been popular among tenants, young professionals, families, and investors, making it one of the emirate's most active communities for both sales and rentals.</p><p>For investors, the appeal lies in Al Reem's rental demand and established residential infrastructure. Unlike some emerging communities, Al Reem already has a strong population base, developed amenities, and regular market activity. This can support long-term rental potential once the project is completed.</p><p>The 40/60 payment plan also makes Tara Park relevant for buyers who prefer to manage payments over time rather than commit the full amount upfront. Payment structures like this are one reason off-plan projects continue to attract strong interest in Abu Dhabi.</p><p>As Abu Dhabi's off-plan market grows, projects in established areas such as Al Reem Island can offer a balance between future development and existing community demand.</p>$html$,
 5, '2026-06-20'::timestamptz, '2026-06-20'::timestamptz, '2026-06-20'::timestamptz),

(gen_random_uuid(), 'abu-dhabi-real-estate-rules-buyer-confidence',
 $t$New Abu Dhabi Real Estate Rules Strengthen Buyer Confidence$t$,
 $e$Abu Dhabi has introduced real estate rules covering escrow accounts, off-plan disputes, and owners' committees to improve transparency.$e$,
 'policy', 'published',
 $html$<p>Abu Dhabi continues to strengthen its real estate framework through new regulations designed to improve transparency, governance, and investor protection. Recent decisions cover areas such as project escrow accounts, jointly owned properties, owners' committees, and procedures related to cancelled off-plan units.</p><p>These updates are important because Abu Dhabi's real estate market is growing quickly. As transaction values rise and more off-plan projects enter the market, clear rules help protect buyers, developers, investors, and owners.</p><p>Escrow regulation is especially important for off-plan buyers. Escrow accounts are used to hold payments made by buyers for a specific development project, helping ensure funds are managed under regulated conditions. ADREC's public guidance describes escrow accounts as secure, regulated bank accounts dedicated to real estate development projects.</p><p>The new framework also addresses owners' committees and jointly owned property management. This matters for buyers in apartment buildings, gated communities, and mixed-use developments, where shared facilities, service charges, and common-area management play a major role in the ownership experience.</p><p>For investors, stronger governance supports market confidence. When buyers feel more protected and regulations are clearer, the market becomes more attractive, especially for long-term and international investors.</p><p>For end-users, these regulations can make the buying process more transparent. Buyers should still review all documents carefully, including the sale and purchase agreement, payment plan, ownership details, service charges, and developer obligations.</p>$html$,
 6, '2026-06-16'::timestamptz, '2026-06-16'::timestamptz, '2026-06-16'::timestamptz),

(gen_random_uuid(), 'abu-dhabi-digital-eoi-off-plan-buyers',
 $t$What Abu Dhabi's Digital EOI System Means for Off-Plan Buyers$t$,
 $e$Abu Dhabi's Madhmoun platform now supports digital registration of off-plan EOIs, improving transparency and investor protection.$e$,
 'policy', 'published',
 $html$<p>Abu Dhabi has introduced digital registration for Expressions of Interest, commonly known as EOIs, for off-plan real estate projects through the Madhmoun platform. The initiative is designed to improve transparency, support investor protection, and regulate the early stages of off-plan buying.</p><p>An EOI is usually submitted by a buyer to show interest in a property before or during a project launch. In many off-plan projects, EOIs are used to reserve buyer interest before unit allocation, booking, or signing the full sale and purchase agreement.</p><p>The digital EOI process helps create a more structured and transparent journey. It allows buyer interest to be recorded through an official platform and supports stronger oversight of payments linked to off-plan project interest. Reports state that the new digital journey through Madhmoun includes mandatory escrow supervision to protect investors.</p><p>This is especially important in a fast-moving market where new launches can attract high demand. A regulated digital process can help buyers feel more confident that their interest and payments are being handled properly.</p><p>For buyers, the key benefit is clarity. Before submitting an EOI, buyers should understand the project, developer, location, expected prices, payment process, refund terms, and next steps after registration.</p><p>For developers and brokers, the system supports a more professional launch process. It helps align off-plan interest with Abu Dhabi's wider goal of improving real estate transparency and investor confidence.</p>$html$,
 6, '2026-06-12'::timestamptz, '2026-06-12'::timestamptz, '2026-06-12'::timestamptz),

(gen_random_uuid(), 'aldar-dmt-abu-dhabi',
 $t$Aldar and DMT to Deliver 9,000 Rental Homes in Abu Dhabi$t$,
 $e$Aldar and Abu Dhabi's DMT will deliver 9,000 value housing rental units in Baniyas and Mohamed Bin Zayed City.$e$,
 'market_report', 'published',
 $html$<p>Abu Dhabi's rental market is set to receive a major supply boost through a partnership between Aldar and the Department of Municipalities and Transport. The two entities announced plans to deliver 9,000 value housing rental units across Baniyas and Mohamed Bin Zayed City.</p><p>The projects form part of Abu Dhabi's Value Housing Programme, which aims to expand access to quality rental housing across the emirate. The developments are expected to support residents looking for more accessible rental options outside the premium island communities.</p><p>Baniyas and Mohamed Bin Zayed City are important residential locations because they offer connectivity, family-friendly surroundings, and access to key roads. The addition of large-scale rental communities may help meet demand from residents seeking practical, well-managed housing.</p><p>For tenants, this type of development could create more choice in the rental market. As Abu Dhabi's population grows and demand increases, value-focused rental communities can help balance affordability with quality.</p><p>For investors and landlords, the announcement also highlights the strength of Abu Dhabi's long-term rental demand. A growing rental population supports the wider property market, especially in communities with strong infrastructure and accessibility.</p><p>This development also reflects a broader trend in Abu Dhabi: the creation of more planned, professionally managed communities that respond to different income levels and lifestyle needs.</p>$html$,
 5, '2026-06-08'::timestamptz, '2026-06-08'::timestamptz, '2026-06-08'::timestamptz),

(gen_random_uuid(), 'yas-island-residential-demand-abu-dhabi',
 $t$Yas Island Continues to Attract Strong Residential Demand$t$,
 $e$Yas Island remains one of Abu Dhabi's most attractive communities, supported by lifestyle amenities, new launches, and strong buyer interest.$e$,
 'field_note', 'published',
 $html$<p>Yas Island continues to stand out as one of Abu Dhabi's strongest residential and lifestyle destinations. Known for its entertainment attractions, waterfront areas, parks, family communities, and growing residential supply, Yas Island appeals to both end-users and investors.</p><p>Aldar's launch of Yas Park Place further reinforces demand for homes in the area. The project is positioned as a new residential community in the heart of Yas Island, set close to parklands, waterfront areas, and major attractions.</p><p>Demand for Yas Island is supported by its lifestyle offering. Residents have access to leisure destinations, retail, hotels, schools, family-friendly facilities, and entertainment venues. This makes the island attractive to families, professionals, and investors seeking long-term rental appeal.</p><p>Yas Island is also growing beyond tourism. New residential communities are helping transform the island into a more complete place to live, not just visit. This shift supports stronger year-round demand and makes the area more attractive for buyers looking for both lifestyle and investment value.</p><p>Recent community investment also supports Yas Island's long-term appeal. The Abu Dhabi Department of Community Development and Aldar announced a partnership to develop Yas Community Park, designed as a new destination for shared experiences and community life.</p><p>For buyers, Yas Island offers a strong mix of apartments, townhouses, villas, and new off-plan projects. For investors, its lifestyle brand and rental demand make it one of Abu Dhabi's key communities to watch.</p>$html$,
 6, '2026-06-04'::timestamptz, '2026-06-04'::timestamptz, '2026-06-04'::timestamptz),

(gen_random_uuid(), 'branded-residences-abu-dhabi-luxury-market',
 $t$Branded Residences Gain Momentum in Abu Dhabi's Luxury Market$t$,
 $e$Branded residences are gaining momentum in Abu Dhabi, with luxury projects such as Manchester City Yas Residences and Baccarat Residences Saadiyat.$e$,
 'luxury', 'published',
 $html$<p>Branded residences are gaining momentum in Abu Dhabi as luxury buyers look for homes connected to globally recognized names, premium design, lifestyle amenities, and exclusive services. This trend is becoming more visible across key destinations such as Yas Island and Saadiyat Island.</p><p>One of the most notable examples is Manchester City Yas Residences by Ohana, a gated waterfront community valued at AED 15 billion. The project marks Manchester City Football Club's first residential development globally and spans approximately 1.67 million square metres.</p><p>The project reflects how branded living is expanding beyond traditional hospitality brands. It combines waterfront living, sports culture, wellness, active lifestyle facilities, and residential design, creating a differentiated offering in Abu Dhabi's luxury market.</p><p>Another major example is Baccarat Residences Saadiyat, launched by Aldar in Abu Dhabi's Saadiyat Cultural District. The project includes 77 homes, including two and three-bedroom apartments, four-bedroom sky villas, and two penthouses.</p><p>For buyers, branded residences offer more than a property. They offer identity, lifestyle, service expectations, exclusivity, and a stronger emotional connection to the home. This can be especially attractive to high-net-worth buyers, international investors, and clients seeking trophy assets.</p><p>For investors, branded residences may also hold long-term appeal because of limited supply, premium positioning, and association with globally recognized names. However, buyers should still evaluate the fundamentals: location, developer reputation, service charges, resale demand, and community growth.</p>$html$,
 7, '2026-05-30'::timestamptz, '2026-05-30'::timestamptz, '2026-05-30'::timestamptz)
on conflict (slug) do nothing;
